Z||000000||mrfiero||05-19-2001||11:47 PM||||It looks like I will be driving to Montgomery, Alabama tomorrow to deliver my 281.5 mile silver Formula to its new owners.  It's kind of sad.......he plans on driving it semi-regularly, so there will be one less low mile Fiero out there (I'll be putting about 1500 miles on it myself!).<P>At any rate, if anyone sees a really nice silver Formula over the next couple of days be sure to wave.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Songman||05-20-2001||02:00 AM||||Take the long way! Come through Nashville and then down I-65!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||05-20-2001||03:07 AM||||Songman,<P>Believe it or not, there is no long way.  It's about 1450 miles whether coming through St. Louis then Nashville or going the southern route through Dallas on over to Alabama.  I plan on taking the first route since I have driven it so often I could do it in my sleep.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'll probably drive through Nashville sometime Tuesday late morning or early afternoon.  I'll honk and wave!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
